{"name":"Elevated","hex":"#b3c3d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elevated","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Raised, usually above ground level.","Increased, particularly above a normal level."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of elevate"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elevated"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elevated (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Elevated is a 1996 Canadian horror-themed short film, directed by Vincenzo Natali and co-written by him and Karen Walton, who also participated in the writing of Ginger Snaps."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/01/Elevated_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elevated_(film)"},{"title":"Elevated railway","blocks":[{"text":"An elevated railway or elevated train is a railway with the tracks above street level on a viaduct or other elevated structure. The railway may be a broad-gauge, standard-gauge or narrow-gauge railway, rapid transit, light rail, monorail, or a suspension railway. Elevated railways are normally found in urban areas that would otherwise require impracticably many level crossings. Usually, the tracks of elevated railways that run on steel viaducts can be seen from street level."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/20220113_03a_CTA_Green_Line_L_near_Congress_St.jpg/330px-20220113_03a_CTA_Green_Line_L_near_Congress_St.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elevated_railway"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Liverpool_Overhead_Railway_-_Every_boy%27s_book_of_railways_and_steamships_%281911%29_%2814572313920%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Liverpool_Overhead_Railway_-_Every_boy%27s_book_of_railways_and_steamships_%281911%29_%2814572313920%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wik